proof.text:
For $\eta:F\Rightarrow G$, use the transformation clause of [lem-pod-texact-truncation-comparison], first for $R$ at $L_{\mathcal C}K$, then for $L$ at $K$. Functoriality of $R_{\mathcal D}$ gives the explicit chain
$$\begin{aligned}
A_{G,K}\eta_{T_{\mathcal C}K}
&=R_{\mathcal D}(a_{G,K})R_{\mathcal D}(\eta_{L_{\mathcal C}K})d_{F,L_{\mathcal C}K}\\
&=R_{\mathcal D}(a_{G,K}\eta_{L_{\mathcal C}K})d_{F,L_{\mathcal C}K}\\
&=R_{\mathcal D}(L_{\mathcal D}(\eta_K)a_{F,K})d_{F,L_{\mathcal C}K}
=T_{\mathcal D}(\eta_K)A_{F,K}.
\end{aligned}$$
Shift compatibility is the assumed equation $c^j_{G,N}\eta_{N[j]}=(\eta_N)[j]c^j_{F,N}$, where $N=T_{\mathcal C}K$. Multiply it on the left by $A_{G,K}[j]$ and substitute the preceding chain. The result is $q_{G,j,K}\eta_{\mathcal H^jK}=\mathcal H^j(\eta_K)q_{F,j,K}$. No invertibility of $\eta$ was used.

